      "created_at": "2025-06-11T05:27:46.272Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hi everyone,</p>\n<p>I’m working on <strong>ERPNext:</strong> v15.61.1, <strong>Frappe HR:</strong> v15.45.2 and I’ve encountered an issue related to <strong>Compensatory Leave Request</strong>.</p>\n<p>I worked <strong>half a day on a holiday</strong>, and the attendance was automatically marked as:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">\"status\": \"Half Day\",\n\"half_day_status\": \"Absent\"\n</code></pre>\n<p>Because of this, I’m unable to apply for a Compensatory Leave — the system throws:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>“You are not present all day(s) between compensatory leave request days”</strong></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This is misleading because I <strong>was present for a half day</strong>, and working hours (5.02) were correctly calculated from check-in/out logs.</p>\n<p>Any guidance or recommended fix is appreciated!</p>",
